1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:02,580
Please insert coins!

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,400
Okay, the magic energy flow is normal.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,877
Boxo, forgive me if this
is none of my business,

4
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:15,597
but if you wish to speak with Lammis,
I'd happily relay your thoughts.

5
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:16,510
That's right.

6
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,537
I could have much deeper
conversations with

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,857
Lammis if I were to rely on Kikuyu's help.

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,900
Thanks, M-O. Understood.

9
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:26,339
Please forgive me if such
a request is presumptuous.

10
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:28,897
It's okay. Thanks!

11
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:33,440
I'm touched, but the first time I really
talk to Lamas, it'll be on my own.

12
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:35,860
There we go, and success!

13
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:39,100
Right, let's proceed through in order.

14
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:41,217
We can start with Kikuyu's group.

15
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:42,130
Perfect.

16
00:00:42,213 --> 00:00:43,413
Thanks so much, Hulani.

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,300
And lastly, it's our turn. Yeah. I'll
activate it. Go ahead. Hello there!

18
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:57,100
What's going on?

19
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:00,040
Whoa, what's with this red light?

20
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,680
This makes no sense.

21
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,877
I found nothing out of
the ordinary with it.

22
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,297
Oh, I don't want to be
away from Botto again.

23
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:08,617
I don't want us to be
apart anymore either.

24
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:11,229
If we could at least
all stay in one group.

25
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:12,570
I know.

26
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:14,260
Activate barrier.

27
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:17,902
Please just let it send
us all to the same place.

28
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:29,937
On the outside I'm just a big metal box
but inside I've still got a human soul.

29
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:32,297
In this new world of
wonders I travel to and

30
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:34,097
fro on the back of my
super strong partner.

31
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:39,160
Llamas the name's Boxo hello
there that means yes by the way.

32
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,980
Boxxo, Hulemy!

33
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,440
I'm glad you're both here. Me too.

34
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:06,280
Thank goodness we're
all together. But where?

35
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,561
I've never seen this room before.

36
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:09,819
This is maddening.

37
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,377
There was nothing wrong
with the transfer circle.

38
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:14,817
And everybody else went
through with no problem.

39
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:15,730
What gives?

40
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:17,110
Uh, Hulemy?

41
00:03:17,193 --> 00:03:20,277
I might be wrong, but I saw something
strange when we transferred.

42
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:23,657
It looked like some kind of red
light coming from on top of Boxo.

43
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:24,570
Huh?

44
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:30,420
Lamas, I owe you one.

45
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:31,940
The malfunction spell.

46
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:34,797
It was cast on Boxo,
not the transfer circle.

47
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:35,977
Wait, what do you mean?

48
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:39,297
There's a damn magic symbol
right here on Boxo's top corner.

49
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:40,457
I'll get rid of it.

50
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:41,837
That's a start, at least.

51
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,840
My top corner? Oh, crap!

52
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,597
That's when it happened!

53
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:46,980
He really got us good.

54
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:50,909
What a pain in the butt to have
as an enemy, that trickster.

55
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:54,318
All right, there should be
no malfunctions next time.

56
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,097
Seems like we'll have
to wait a few days for

57
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:58,886
the Transfer Circle's
magic power to recharge.

58
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:01,201
Huh, this is the seventh stratum.

59
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:04,540
Um, so is that the Dark Forest Stratum?

60
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:09,447
Yeah, I hear it's a pretty dangerous
place inhabited by lots of plant monsters.

61
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:13,311
Although from the look of
things, nothing's been destroyed.

62
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:14,410
What?

63
00:04:14,493 --> 00:04:17,118
Why is a tree growing right
in front of the entrance?

64
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,737
And the way it's shaped, it looks like...

65
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:22,040
It looks like a person. How creepy.

66
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,740
Creepy is right.

67
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:27,917
I've heard that there are monsters on
this stratum that turn people into trees.

68
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,817
It's bad news for women,
children, and the elderly.

69
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,397
People who can't put up a fight.

70
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:35,245
Hearing that, it's even
harder to look at them.

71
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,600
Someone must be here. Over there.

72
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,951
I'll happily deal with the carrot beanies.

73
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:55,509
These monsters' bodily
fluids can be toxic.

74
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:58,337
If any gets on your boots, I
shall clean them off later.

75
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:00,832
I've been wanting to fight some monsters!

76
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,480
Your help is appreciated.

77
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:05,350
Ubuntu!

78
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,697
I've been waiting for you!

79
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:09,900
Please don't shake too hard! Shwing!

80
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:11,220
Calm down!

81
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:20,337
I almost forgot how good his meat is.

82
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:21,337
You ain't kidding.

83
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:22,797
It's nice to have meat again.

84
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:23,877
I'm so sick of veggies.

85
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:28,257
This place is naturally verdant all around
a field bursting with vegetables aplenty.

86
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:30,575
Meat, however, is surprisingly scarce.

87
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:31,810
Aha!

88
00:05:31,893 --> 00:05:33,760
No wonder they're wolfing it down.

89
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,060
Mishuel isn't with you? He's not.

90
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:39,537
Only Shui and I were sent
to this stratum, apparently.

91
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:40,450
Interesting.

92
00:05:40,533 --> 00:05:43,917
Well, with Mishuel's strength, he's
probably fine, no matter where he went.

93
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,980
It's weird.

94
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,597
With all these people turned into trees,

95
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,857
you'd think at least some
houses would be destroyed.

96
00:05:48,940 --> 00:05:52,577
The monsters of this stratum are extremely
reluctant to harm any vegetation,

97
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:53,719
even felled trees.

98
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:56,757
I imagine they consider the
wood planks kindred beings.

99
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:57,670
That's crazy!

100
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,697
Then I guess that means
they get really angry

101
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:01,477
when you cut down trees to build a house,

102
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,390
doesn't it?

103
00:06:02,473 --> 00:06:03,303
It does indeed.

104
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:06,717
Apparently you must go to great
pains here to cut down even one.

105
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,817
Those strange trees we saw in the
village, were they once people?

106
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:10,730
Yes.

107
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:12,137
Those are the women, children,

108
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:14,597
and people of a certain
age who inhaled the Stratum

109
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,157
Lord's pollen during a
previous monster attack.

110
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,593
It's horrifying to see.

111
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,947
I'm shocked anyone survived.

112
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,337
Stratum Lords are formidable.

113
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:23,417
Did they defeat it?

114
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:24,600
Oh, heavens no.

115
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,597
They merely drove it away with fire,

116
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:30,577
but they only use it as a threat for
fear it could burn down the village.

117
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:31,580
Oh, I see.

118
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:35,217
I recall fire being banned on this
stratum, so that does make sense.

119
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,200
Indeed it does.

120
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:38,897
They could easily defeat
the Stratum Lord with fire.

121
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:43,333
But the trees of this stratum are
especially vulnerable to heat and flame.

122
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:46,937
The people who turned into trees,
is there a way to turn them back?

123
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:49,726
I believe so, if the
stratum lord is defeated.

124
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:50,801
Oh, that's good.

125
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:53,597
But it seems like it
would be really hard to

126
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:56,504
find a stratum lord in a
giant forest like this.

127
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:59,940
Actually, finding the stratum
lord is the easiest part.

128
00:07:00,580 --> 00:07:01,620
That's it there.

129
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,580
Huh? What?

130
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,540
That giant tree guy?

131
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,657
That thing looks taller than a skyscraper!

132
00:07:07,740 --> 00:07:11,357
How does that thing ambulate without
crushing all the trees in the forest?

133
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:14,697
I believe that's one of the
Stratum Lord's powers, in fact.

134
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:17,777
When it does move, all the
trees scamper out of the way.

135
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:21,154
A Stratum Lord that can control
plants in a forest, huh?

136
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:23,857
That doesn't sound like
it'd be easy to deal with.

137
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:26,737
We can delve further into
that subject tomorrow.

138
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:28,055
Look at our comrades.

139
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,772
They're in no condition.

140
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:31,800
I can't eat anymore.

141
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,960
I'd say Shui won't be
of any use for a while.

142
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:38,739
I guess that means guard
duty is up to us right now.

143
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,430
You know,

144
00:07:42,513 --> 00:07:46,197
it feels like it's been forever since you
and I got to be alone together like this.

145
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:49,157
Now that you mention it,
it does feel like forever.

146
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:52,217
This might be kind of weird
to say, so don't get mad.

147
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:56,157
But I have this feeling that I can
do anything as long as I'm with you.

148
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,720
Aw, thanks, Lamas.

149
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:59,036
I feel that way too.

150
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:00,670
Yes, thanks!

151
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:04,435
Thanks seems like an odd thing to say.

152
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:06,410
Huh?

153
00:08:06,493 --> 00:08:08,560
What's with this deep, tender vibe?

154
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:10,870
Whoa.

155
00:08:10,953 --> 00:08:12,160
Uh, Lamas?

156
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,070
Wait a minute.

157
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:16,637
Um, what's happening? Is she...

158
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:19,297
Don't tell me this is the
start of a kitschy rom-com

159
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:22,498
between an inanimate object
and his girl best friend!

160
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:29,040
Oh right, I forgot we
were on watch. Too bad.

161
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:31,457
Yeah, we gotta take it seriously.

162
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:32,370
Whoa!

163
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:35,557
You're telling me you've been
eating these monsters lately?

164
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,470
That's right.

165
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:39,617
The vegetable monsters here actually
taste pretty good in their own way.

166
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:41,053
A little gamey, though.

167
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,190
Besides,

168
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:44,717
there's plenty of lumber around here,

169
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:47,800
so luckily I won't run out
of arrows any time soon.

170
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,230
Shui!

171
00:08:49,313 --> 00:08:51,880
As requested, I brought
you more arrows. Thanks!

172
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:53,300
You got it.

173
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:57,519
Oh, that's Boxo on your back, so
you must be the blessing of my girl.

174
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,597
The name is Lamas.

175
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:02,040
Oh, okay, then. Sorry about that.

176
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:05,157
Rumor has it that you
fight bare-handed, Lamas.

177
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,070
Is that true?

178
00:09:06,153 --> 00:09:07,218
Yeah, that's right.

179
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:10,077
Well, that seems like a waste
for your blessing of might.

180
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:11,572
Come on over to my shop.

181
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,701
I'll find you a damn good weapon.

182
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:16,210
Oh!

183
00:09:16,293 --> 00:09:18,460
So this is an otherworldly weapons shop.

184
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:20,972
But, like, I don't even need any weapons.

185
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,337
It can't hurt to look.

186
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:26,417
And he said you could have whatever
you want as thanks for Boxo's food.

187
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:27,330
Ha-ha!

188
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,377
I knew there'd be all kinds of cool stuff.

189
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:33,340
Huh, I'm surprised to see some
with magic stones built into them.

190
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:36,340
So, my friends, what do
you think of my shop?

191
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,958
Feel free to browse at your leisure.

192
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:41,160
What's this? Oh, that one?

193
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:42,660
It's water repellent.

194
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:45,677
Good in the hot or cold,
and it performs wonderfully.

195
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,100
But it's also flashy.

196
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,560
And it's not for sale.

197
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:52,180
What do you think, Boxo?

198
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:53,840
Thank you very much.

199
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,160
Hold on a sec.

200
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:56,877
Did you just give me a compliment?

201
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:57,790
Yes.

202
00:09:58,740 --> 00:09:59,620
Thank you.

203
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:02,557
I'm really surprised by
how good it looks on her.

204
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:05,477
But then, just about anything
would look good on Lamas.

205
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:09,077
Oh, I think we should try to
get him to sell it to us later.

206
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:11,940
Now then, this one's a type of magic item.

207
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:14,968
They get heavier the
moment you pick one up.

208
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:16,554
Measuring stones, huh?

209
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:19,497
That's a pretty unusual
magic item you've got there.

210
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:20,957
You sure know your stuff.

211
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:21,900
Well, go on.

212
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,889
Try it out, why don't you?

213
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,057
Oh, it's so light.

214
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:28,022
Nah, you just make it look easy.

215
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,777
Want to try holding it, Hulemy?

216
00:10:29,860 --> 00:10:30,700
Sure, why not?

217
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:31,710
Hand it over.

218
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,270
Oh!

219
00:10:33,353 --> 00:10:34,183
Lama's taking it!

220
00:10:34,266 --> 00:10:36,140
Take it now! Ah! Close call.

221
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,397
There was almost a hole in the floor.

222
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,009
Okay, let's skip over one.

223
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:41,806
Try and pick up number three.

224
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:43,714
Whoa, are you serious?

225
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,240
Yeah, this one is super light, too.

226
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:49,072
Well, how about the one at the end, then?

227
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:53,277
It's about as heavy as Boxo. Really?

228
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,838
This is incredible!

229
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,837
You're even stronger than I thought!

230
00:10:58,920 --> 00:10:59,750
Right!

231
00:10:59,833 --> 00:11:02,013
I'm gonna make you your ultimate weapon!

232
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:04,040
I hope you're ready! Dang!

233
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:07,237
This weapons merchant guy
is practically on fire!

234
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:10,380
You really do that? Heck yeah! I'm on it!

235
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:15,540
You know, we have yet to meet
the director of this stratum.

236
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:18,197
We dropped by the
Hunters Association right

237
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,751
away when we went to all the other strata.

238
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:29,040
Do I know Director Dark?

239
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,857
No, I haven't met him as a matter of fact.

240
00:11:31,940 --> 00:11:33,940
Lamas, do you know what he's like?

241
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:38,580
Well, let me see.

242
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,840
I would characterize
him as cheerful and fun.

243
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,257
He's a good fit for
the Stratum's director.

244
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:46,660
Yeah, he's not a bad guy by any means.

245
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:50,480
What are these two not telling us?

246
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:55,136
If you're curious about the director,
this might be the perfect timing.

247
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,580
Hey, nice to meet ya!

248
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,797
You can call me Director Dark if you like!

249
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:02,437
Honestly, I'd be thrilled if
you just remembered my face!

250
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:05,457
I mean, how many guys do you have
me who look like a creepy shadow?!

251
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:07,497
That's the part where
you're supposed to laugh.

252
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:08,957
Darkness Fiend's my race, you see.

253
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:12,257
That sounds all impressive, but my
vibe's all about having fun, bro!

254
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:13,797
I'm a real party guy at heart!

255
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:16,137
I might be a Darkness Fiend,
but I like to keep things light!

256
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:19,797
My days are all hectic and messy
thinking about it makes me tired.

257
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:23,057
I gotta sit down But it's my opinion
that as director I've got to do

258
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:26,177
my best to be dignified no matter
how much it goes against my nature.

259
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:28,897
Oh, yeah You guys are from
Clearflow Lake Stratum, right?

260
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:30,477
How's that cuddly director bear doing?

261
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:31,517
I bet he keeps busy,

262
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:35,482
too Doesn't he say every day is
just a turtle bear to get through?

263
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:42,437
He talks like a man's eye performer
and this hail of cheesy jokes

264
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:46,377
is denting my surface I would
characterize him as cheerful and fun.

265
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:48,657
He's a good fit for
the Stratum's director.

266
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:50,720
He's not a bad guy by any means.

267
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:54,627
That explains why those two
didn't come along to introduce us.

268
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:58,340
Hey, Boxo, why so stiff?
You nervous? Hey, loosen up!

269
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,838
Oh, I guess you're always the stiff.

270
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,737
From what I'm told, Boxo
dispenses unusual food and drink.

271
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,937
Now that's what I call a magical item.

272
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:07,850
What's that you say?

273
00:13:07,933 --> 00:13:08,917
I should try it for myself.

274
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,657
Don't mind if I do it, much obliged.

275
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:13,277
I don't want to encourage him,
but this guy's a director.

276
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:15,301
I guess I have to be nice to him.

277
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:19,377
You really can make stuff
float through the air!

278
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:20,460
Just spectacular!

279
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:23,211
Never had a floating machine drink before.

280
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:26,798
That's tasty stuff.

281
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:27,937
Like, really tasty.

282
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:29,957
More than I'd expect from sweet tea.

283
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:32,537
Now if only I had a
sweet tea pie by my side!

284
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:33,450
Get it!

285
00:13:33,533 --> 00:13:34,363
Big mistake.

286
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:38,697
I'll have to listen to dad jokes forever
if I don't do something, and quickly.

287
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:41,074
There's gotta be some way to outdo him.

288
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:42,340
I've got it!

289
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,250
Form change!

290
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:47,140
A manzai vending machine.

291
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:48,840
What's happening?

292
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,030
Hello, people.

293
00:13:50,113 --> 00:13:50,943
How are you?

294
00:13:51,026 --> 00:13:52,137
Hey, full house tonight.

295
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,877
Thank you for coming
out to see us, friend.

296
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:54,897
Look at that front row.

297
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,417
We got a pretty girl, pretty girl.

298
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:57,330
Oh, skip that one.

299
00:13:57,413 --> 00:13:59,040
Pretty girl? Cut that out.

300
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:02,437
I ever tell you about how my mom
can't remember her favorite novel?

301
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:03,437
Huh, maybe I can help.

302
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:04,350
What is it about?

303
00:14:04,433 --> 00:14:06,097
The main character goes to another world.

304
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:09,517
Oh, sure, when a guy goes to
another world, that's an easy guy.

305
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:12,129
Watch and learn from
the old school, buddy.

306
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:14,657
Nothing easy about it, friend.

307
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:16,457
He's a difficult guy
having a real hard time.

308
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:17,370
What a coincidence.

309
00:14:17,453 --> 00:14:19,617
I'm also having a hard
time with a typical guy.

310
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:20,876
Thank you very much.

311
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,520
Thanks for coming out today, folks.

312
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,940
Hopefully this puts him
in his place for a while.

313
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,010
Huh?

314
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,174
We'll fell some trees to create a path.

315
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:39,937
If the monsters seem too
dangerous, we'll come right back.

316
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:43,667
Our goal this time is to measure
how powerful the enemies are.

317
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:47,246
Here comes our grand welcome.

318
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:49,365
Shall we deal with them first?

319
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:51,120
Like you even have to ask.

320
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:54,620
He seems like a total joker,

321
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:57,797
but apparently Director Dark used to
be in the same group as Director Bear?

322
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,257
so they fought side by side.

323
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:02,222
I bet he's pretty handy
in a fight, goofy or not.

324
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:07,137
I don't recall putting
veggies on my chopping list.

325
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:11,161
For the sake of my sanity, I'm
going to pretend I didn't hear that.

326
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:17,037
Lamas, there are fewer enemies now.

327
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,957
Please remove some of the trees.

328
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:19,870
Okay!

329
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,920
Oh, that's an amazing sight!

330
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,377
I'm just getting started!

331
00:15:34,460 --> 00:15:35,519
Let's get started!

332
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:40,060
Lamas, let's call it a
day and head back. Okay!

333
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,577
That's how we spent the next few days,

334
00:15:42,660 --> 00:15:46,013
clearing trees and extending
the path through the forest.

335
00:15:52,180 --> 00:15:55,377
We've covered a lot of ground,
but there's been no movement.

336
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:59,257
I'm beginning to think it might be
faster to just go look for the commander.

337
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:00,420
Oh, there you are.

338
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:02,237
I've been looking for you.

339
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:06,800
Botan, Kuroyata, and Director
Baron Kikuyu! Hey, friends!

340
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,471
Whoa, how'd you get here?

341
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:11,857
I thought the transfer circle wouldn't
be usable for two or three days.

342
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:13,817
You want to know how we got here?

343
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:16,897
Well, the flow of magic power
seems to have settled a bit?

344
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:19,137
So I tried directing
it from the other side.

345
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:21,997
and I was able to activate
the transfer circle that way.

346
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,320
Wow, not a bad idea.

347
00:16:23,660 --> 00:16:26,137
But it would take someone
with your skill to do it.

348
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:28,520
Skill is one upside of growing old.

349
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:30,465
It's been a long time, ma 'am.

350
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:33,548
Well, well, it's the
girl with the appetite.

351
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:35,211
Shui is your name, yes?

352
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:37,997
I'm sure that mess with
the captain was difficult.

353
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:40,497
Don't worry, I put all that behind me now.

354
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:42,597
My butt's asleep, are we there yet?

355
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:44,327
Yeah, and is it time to eat?

356
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:47,677
Shirley said lack of sleep
is the arch enemy of beauty.

357
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:48,677
What's that mean?

358
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:51,137
They even have the band
of gluttons with them.

359
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:52,997
Now Team Traveling Zoo is complete.

360
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:56,360
All the soft, cozy animal
time one could ever want.

361
00:16:57,820 --> 00:17:01,317
All right, it's time to face the
music and go see Black Black.

362
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:02,230
Huh?

363
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:04,100
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

364
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:06,237
My back pain just started flurrying
up out of nowhere in the match page.

365
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:07,150
Are you okay, Gramps?

366
00:17:07,233 --> 00:17:09,377
I'm so sorry, but I need to tend to him.

367
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:10,290
I'm afraid I won't be able to...

368
00:17:10,373 --> 00:17:11,557
Don't even try it, you two.

369
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,537
Come on, you both know I
can't deal with him alone.

370
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:16,660
Ah, he means Director Dark.

371
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:18,161
Let's head back.

372
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:20,410
Fine.

373
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,680
Kikoyu, take care of you-know-what.

374
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,320
Yes, I'd be honored to. Huh?

375
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:28,052
What was that all about?

376
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:31,900
Boxxo, Director Bear asked me for a favor.

377
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,613
Would you mind helping?

378
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:35,180
A favor?

379
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:37,977
The people currently in this village.

380
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:40,001
Is that everyone on this stratum?

381
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:41,350
That's right.

382
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:45,677
It's about time for me to distribute food,
so I think they're all going to gather.

383
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:50,172
Then as we discussed before, I will
hand out your products to each of them.

384
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:52,160
Hello there!

385
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:53,480
Here you are.

386
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:56,460
Um, your name is Kikoyu, isn't it?

387
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:57,700
Well, thank you.

388
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,449
Thanks a lot, little lady.

389
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,160
Here you are.

390
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:08,140
I've figured out what Kikoyu has in mind.

391
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,420
Here you are.

392
00:18:14,140 --> 00:18:14,970
Right!

393
00:18:15,053 --> 00:18:16,180
I'll record her face.

394
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:19,397
Kikoyu was reading minds
as she handed over the

395
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:22,237
box lunches in order to
search for the commander.

396
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:23,150
This person.

397
00:18:23,233 --> 00:18:25,220
She is the Netherlord's commander.

398
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,471
That's one of my hunters!

399
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:30,877
That youngster's been working
hard here on this stratum,

400
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,666
and I had high hopes for her!

401
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:36,820
I had no idea she was working
for the Netherlord! I see,

402
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:40,817
but we don't know whether she was hiding
it all along or was persuaded to defect.

403
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:43,380
Now then, what do we do next?

404
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:47,097
We should get information out
of her immediately, but how?

405
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:48,240
Oh, I know!

406
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:50,380
We have just the man for the job.

407
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:56,620
That is an option.

408
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:00,577
Heavy, we would like you to
arrest and question the commander.

409
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,477
Do you have any thoughts about that?

410
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:03,800
Ah, yes, I see.

411
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:05,180
I'd be happy to.

412
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:10,304
I can use hallucinations to gather
information, or perhaps affect her emotionally.

413
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:11,390
Well,

414
00:19:11,473 --> 00:19:15,117
when it comes to apprehending the villain,
you'd better leave the arrest up to me.

415
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:19,435
This scandal happened on my watch,
so it's up to me to set things right.

416
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:27,158
I couldn't read his expression, but
I could sense he was really angry.

417
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:30,520
As director, I imagine he
wants to clean up this mess.

418
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:33,639
Actually, anyone know where she is?

419
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,840
Okay, here she comes.

420
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:44,260
This room's well soundproofed.

421
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:46,187
Nobody's going to hear this.

422
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,386
Hey, boss, take it from here.

423
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:52,137
I will use my sensory manipulation
to deactivate her sense

424
00:19:52,220 --> 00:19:55,197
of touch and pain and make
her believe she is dreaming.

425
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:58,717
I will alter her vision to make
her think she sees the netherlord,

426
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:03,565
but she will still be able to hear, so
please refrain from speaking while I work.

427
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:08,336
If her sense of touch is muted, she
won't know if somebody touches her.

428
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:15,477
I am speaking to you in your dream.

429
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:17,160
Can you tell who I am?

430
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:20,000
The Netherlord.

431
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:21,850
Whoa!

432
00:20:21,933 --> 00:20:24,057
He must really appear to
her as the Netherlord!

433
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:28,905
Then recount for me the circumstances
under which you first began working for me.

434
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:30,940
Yes, sir.

435
00:20:31,260 --> 00:20:35,340
About two months ago, you
appeared before me as a human.

436
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:37,400
You said if I obeyed you,

437
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:41,137
you'd give me enough money
to pay off my gambling debt

438
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:44,740
and live the rest of my
life without having to work.

439
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:47,340
What did I tell you to do?

440
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:51,120
While purporting to defend
the people as a hunter,

441
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:54,720
I would use this ring to
order the monsters to attack.

442
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:57,631
Correct, and is that all you can remember?

443
00:20:58,080 --> 00:21:02,620
About two weeks ago, I met with
members of the Menagerie of Fools,

444
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:04,220
new recruits of yours.

445
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:06,815
They seemed to be looking for someone,

446
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,737
but they left as soon as they
realized they weren't here.

447
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:12,644
So the captain and crew
dropped by this stratum.

448
00:21:12,900 --> 00:21:16,841
They were probably looking for the
two remaining Menagerie members.

449
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,420
One last thing.

450
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:22,557
Could you take off those
boots and show them to me?

451
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:25,377
Bro, don't forget you're
the Netherlord right now!

452
00:21:25,460 --> 00:21:27,600
Um, you want my boots?

453
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:31,840
For some strange reason, I'm
finding it difficult to move.

454
00:21:32,140 --> 00:21:34,257
Then I shall carefully remove them myself,

455
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:38,480
so that the scent gradually wafts
out and makes its way to my nose!

456
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:40,590
Director.

457
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:42,740
This is rich.

458
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:45,137
You've always had a problem with gambling.

459
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:48,500
But I always thought you could change!

460
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:52,900
When I'd loaned you money before,
you said you'd never gamble again!

461
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:55,480
I'm a dope for believing you!

462
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:59,880
Well then, that takes
care of the Commander.

463
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:04,680
All we've got left now is to turn
those trees back into people.

464
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:19,500
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

465
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:25,500
It's not my journey.

466
00:22:27,100 --> 00:22:27,930
It's broken.

467
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:31,980
It's still not there.

468
00:22:33,860 --> 00:22:36,320
I've got a letter to the letter.

469
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:39,286
I've got a letter to the air.

470
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:40,510
I've got a letter to the air.

471
00:22:40,593 --> 00:22:43,180
I've got a letter to the air.

472
00:23:34,860 --> 00:23:39,620
you could even win a reward i
look forward to serving you again
